def c(i,key,value,why,src=[s],option=None):qe(q,'secf-principles-q'+str(i),key,value,why,src,option)
e('Web app credentials: ALL PRIVILEGES\n  attacker gets SQLi -> drops every table,\n  reads every schema, creates users','Web app has broad database authority\n  SQLi may read/alter/drop accessible data;\n  extra role powers depend on the DB','ALL table privileges do not grant every database/admin role power.')
e('  attacker gets SQLi -> reads orders\n  (bad, but contained)','  SQLi may read orders/products,\n  insert orders (still serious)','Restricteddiagram omitted granted INSERT and product SELECT.')
e('- **Drop privileges after start-up.** A server binds to port 443 as root, then switches to an unprivileged user. Containers run as non-root.','- **Avoid unnecessary elevated execution.** Use an unprivileged service with a narrowly scoped binding mechanism where supported. If start-up needs elevation, drop the unneeded identities, groups and capabilities afterwards. Non-root containers still need appropriate capability and access controls.','Avoid universal root for443 and incomplete drop.')
e('> An attacker used a server-side request forgery flaw in a misconfigured web application firewall to obtain the instance\'s cloud credentials. Those credentials could list and read a large number of S3 buckets, exposing data on around 100 million people. A role scoped to what the firewall actually needed would have turned a breach into a minor incident.','> Capital One reported unauthorised access affecting approximately 100 million individuals in the US and six million in Canada. The company identified a configuration vulnerability. The exact exploit chain and the counterfactual claim that a narrower role would have made the incident minor are not established by the disclosure used here, so those details are omitted.','Use primary reported scope and omit unsupported counterfactual.',[cap])
e('The picture safety engineers use is the **Swiss cheese model**: each layer has holes, but the holes rarely line up.','A layered design should account for gaps and shared failure modes instead of assuming that several controls guarantee protection.','Remove unsupported holealignmentfrequency.')
e('Two controls that share a failure mode (the same library, the same credential, the same admin) are really one control.','Controls sharing a failure mode (a library, credential or administration path) can fail together for that threat, even if they provide different protections elsewhere.','Correlation does not makecontrolsidenticalforallthreats.')
e('every request is authenticated and authorised regardless of where it comes from.','network location alone does not confer trust, and access decisions use the relevant identity, device and resource policy. This does not require a fresh interactive login for every request.','Correct zero trust simplification.',[z])
e("For a fire door's magnetic lock, yes: **fail open**, because the availability of the exit outweighs everything else. Make the choice deliberately, per system, rather than letting an unhandled exception decide.","Other systems may have a different safety or availability requirement. Physical exit and fire-containment design requires its own safety rules and is not specified here. Make the access-control failure policy explicit instead of letting an unhandled exception decide.",'Do not confuse unlockedegress withopenfiredoor orprescribeunverifiedsafety.')
e('Fix by checking and using the same handle.','Use appropriate credentials when opening the object and validate the opened object through its handle. A handle prevents that name-substitution race, but does not itself establish permission or make the object immutable.','Handle alone notfull authorization.',[f])
e('A protection mechanism that needs **two keys** is stronger than one that needs one.','A protection mechanism can require **two independent conditions**, so compromise of one condition is insufficient. Benefits depend on independence and correct enforcement.','Not universal stronger guarantee.')
e('The fix is to make the deputy act with the caller\'s authority, not its own.','Restrict what authority the deputy may exercise for each caller. For URL fetching, validate destinations and redirects, constrain network access and avoid exposing unnecessary credentials.','Caller authority notalwaysdirectlyavailableforSSRF.',[ss])
e('- Open design: assume attackers can read your code; only keys should be secret.','- Open design: do not depend on hiding the mechanism. Protect keys, credentials and sensitive data independently.','Onlykeyssecret overlyexclusive.')
c(1,'explanation','Correct. The requested permissions are much narrower than s3:*. Other policies, explicit denies and encryption-key access can still constrain effective access, but the broad grant is unnecessary.','IAMallow notall effectiveaccess.',[a,'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html'],3)
c(1,'workedExample','GetObject on the input objects and PutObject on the output objects use object ARNs such as arn:aws:s3:::input-bucket/* and arn:aws:s3:::output-bucket/*, not just bucket ARNs. Add only other required operations, such as listing or encryption-key use, after checking the workflow. Evaluate the complete effective policy, including explicit denies.','BucketARN wrongforobjectactions.',[a])
c(2,'explanation','Not generally equivalent. A allows every role except guest; B allows only admin and analyst. They differ for any other role.','Existingrolesneednotagree.',option=2)
c(3,'prompt','An admin panel has no authentication other than an unpublished, short fixed path, /x7q-admin. Its designers assume nobody will discover the path. Which principle does this violate?','Not unguessable, distinguishcapabilityURL.')
c(3,'explanation','Correct. Hiding a short fixed route is not a robust credential design; it can be discovered or disclosed. Open design asks whether the protection still works when the mechanism is known.','URLs can be bearercredentialsifdesignedso.',option=0)
c(3,'explanation','Purpose-built capability URLs can carry high-entropy bearer secrets, with careful scope, expiry and disclosure controls. This short fixed admin route is not such a design.','Do not declareallURLs nonauthenticators.',option=3)
c(4,'explanation','A generic method-blocking rule cannot replace the application permission decision. A gateway could enforce trusted identity-aware policy, but that must actually be configured and complete.','WAFcanhaveidentitycontext.',option=3)
c(5,'text','Allows this check to pass on timeout; fail open, potentially bypassing authorisation','Othercontrols maystilldeny.',option=2)
c(5,'explanation','Fail-open can be intentional for a particular operation, but it is not universally correct. The appropriate failure policy follows the system requirements and threat model.','Removefireexitoversimplification.',option=3)
c(6,'explanation','Correct as complementary layers. A private subnet limits direct database access; parameterised queries protect the application query path. An attacker using the app need not bypass the subnet separately, because the app already has database access.','Not everypath traverses everycontrol.',option=0)
c(6,'explanation','Correct as complementary controls. MFA can reduce account takeover risk; authorisation constrains permitted actions. MFA does not stop every stolen-session or phishing attack.','MFA not universalcredentialtheftdefense.',option=2)
c(6,'workedExample','Assess layers against particular paths and shared dependencies. Subnet isolation helps against direct database exposure while query parameterisation helps against injection through an authorised app connection. Identical WAF rules can share bypasses. MFA, permission checks, encryption and detection address different risks but still depend on configuration and enforcement. Browser-only validation cannot enforce server policy.','Correct conjunction and independence assumptions.')
c(8,'explanation','Correct. An attacker-controlled pathname can resolve to a different object between calls. Open under appropriately reduced user/group/capability authority; retain and use that descriptor. Merely opening as root and keeping the descriptor does not establish the caller was authorised.','Descriptor alone insufficientfix.',[f],1)
c(9,'prompt','In an EC2 deployment allowing IMDSv1, an unrestricted server-side URL fetch can return credentials from the instance metadata endpoint at http://169.254.169.254/. Which framing best describes the flaw?','Specificcloud/configurationassumptions.',[im,ss])
c(9,'workedExample','An attacker can cause the server to fetch data reachable from its own network context. Restrict schemes and destinations, resolve and check all applicable addresses, and validate or disable redirects; protect against DNS changes between validation and connection. Requiring IMDSv2 reduces exposure to many simple SSRF paths, but is not a complete SSRF defence. Use least privilege and network restrictions as additional controls.','IMDSv2 notuniversalsolution DNSredirectgaps.',[im,ss])
c(10,'text','Prevent shared caching of personalised responses, or use a safely authenticated cache key covering every relevant authorisation context','Tenantalone insufficientper-userdashboard.',[cache],3)
c(10,'explanation','Correct. Cache-Control: private directs conforming shared caches not to store the response. A partitioned key must distinguish all users/permissions that change the representation, not merely tenants.','Tenantnotallpersonalization.',[cache],3)
c(10,'workedExample','If both requests match the same stored response, B can receive A\'s data. Use private, no-store where storage is inappropriate, or a deliberate cache design that authenticates before reuse and keys every relevant tenant/user/permission context. Do not trust a client-supplied tenant header alone. Clear already stored sensitive entries when fixing the design.','Addresssame-tenantleaks spoofedkeys and existingcache.',[cache])
c(11,'explanation','Correct. Properly enforced separation prevents one ordinary account from completing both steps. It does not prove fraud needs human collusion: an attacker might compromise both approvers or bypass the workflow.','Nounsupportedcollusionlikelihood.',option=1)
